WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.820 --> 00:00:03.989
That wall that I have right there

00:00:03.990 --> 00:00:05.219
would have been the mission wall

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:06.329
that surrounded the Alamo.

00:00:06.330 --> 00:00:08.579
And that's the wall that the Mexican

00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:09.869
troops hit.

00:00:09.870 --> 00:00:12.149
I'm right in the battlefield of why

00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:13.889
Texas is Texas.

00:00:13.890 --> 00:00:16.229
Vince Cantu runs Moses Rose's,

00:00:16.230 --> 00:00:18.089
a San Antonio, Texas, bar

00:00:18.090 --> 00:00:19.679
that's on the site of the famous

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:21.959
1836 battle memorialized

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:23.759
on the big screen many times by the

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:25.499
likes of John Wayne and Billy Bob

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:26.579
Thornton.

00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:28.919
He opened Moses Rose's in 2010

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:30.629
after it had sat vacant for many

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:31.799
years.

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:33.479
My family's been here for four

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:35.129
generations running taverns downtown

00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:36.179
San Antonio.

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:37.559
I'm proud of my family.

00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:39.629
My great grandfather had a tavern

00:00:39.630 --> 00:00:40.619
four blocks that way.

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:41.909
My grandmother had a restaurant.

00:00:41.910 --> 00:00:43.319
My grandfather had a restaurant less

00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:44.489
than a quarter mile that way.

00:00:44.490 --> 00:00:45.779
I feel like I am on the shoulders of

00:00:45.780 --> 00:00:47.459
giants. I like what I do and I like

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:48.419
where I do it.

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:49.919
I never really thought about it

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:51.509
happening to me until it happened to

00:00:51.510 --> 00:00:52.919
me. I've been living under the

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:54.239
threat of eminent domain for six

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:55.240
years.

00:00:55.640 --> 00:00:57.529
The Alamo Trust, a nonprofit

00:00:57.530 --> 00:00:59.119
that manages the site, wants to

00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:01.069
expand the Alamo Museum, which

00:01:01.070 --> 00:01:02.539
would include building a theater and

00:01:02.540 --> 00:01:04.249
a civil rights exhibit where Moses

00:01:04.250 --> 00:01:06.109
Rose's currently stands.

00:01:06.110 --> 00:01:08.119
Cantu says that in 2016,

00:01:08.120 --> 00:01:09.679
the group made its first offer of

00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:11.569
$1,000,000 signed by

00:01:11.570 --> 00:01:13.999
then–Land Commissioner George Bush,

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:15.439
which would have barely covered his

00:01:15.440 --> 00:01:16.729
outstanding loans.

00:01:16.730 --> 00:01:18.629
Four years later, they upped it to 2

00:01:18.630 --> 00:01:19.609
million.

00:01:19.610 --> 00:01:21.379
And I've told them no both times.

00:01:21.380 --> 00:01:23.329
Mostly because, you know, I'm

00:01:23.330 --> 00:01:25.039
60 years old and it puts me out of a

00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:26.599
job, come back in ten years and see

00:01:26.600 --> 00:01:27.829
what it's worth. And maybe, maybe

00:01:27.830 --> 00:01:28.729
that's the way I want to do it,

00:01:28.730 --> 00:01:29.929
because I'm not gonna, I'm not gonna

00:01:29.930 --> 00:01:31.849
look at ten year money at 3% a year

00:01:31.850 --> 00:01:33.289
when it's been appreciating at,

00:01:33.290 --> 00:01:35.359
like, 18% a year.

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:37.939
At the outset, the $400-million

00:01:37.940 --> 00:01:39.529
museum-expansion project was

00:01:39.530 --> 00:01:41.449
supposed to be paid for by private

00:01:41.450 --> 00:01:42.289
donors.

00:01:42.290 --> 00:01:43.969
When the funding fell through, the

00:01:43.970 --> 00:01:45.859
state of Texas stepped in to cover

00:01:45.860 --> 00:01:46.849
the cost.

00:01:46.850 --> 00:01:48.649
The state made two more offers,

00:01:48.650 --> 00:01:50.209
which Cantu rejected.

00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:52.279
He said he'd sell for 15 million.

00:01:52.280 --> 00:01:54.169
So state officials who declined

00:01:54.170 --> 00:01:56.149
to participate in this story,

00:01:56.150 --> 00:01:57.799
countered by threatening to take his

00:01:57.800 --> 00:01:59.719
property by force using eminent

00:01:59.720 --> 00:02:00.709
domain.

00:02:00.710 --> 00:02:02.599
Cantu would receive a so-called

00:02:02.600 --> 00:02:04.519
fair market price based on

00:02:04.520 --> 00:02:06.319
an independent appraiser's estimate

00:02:06.320 --> 00:02:08.209
of the property's current value.

00:02:08.210 --> 00:02:10.059
The appraisal came in at 2.1

00:02:10.060 --> 00:02:12.209
million, or roughly 2.8

00:02:12.210 --> 00:02:14.239
million in ten years.

00:02:14.240 --> 00:02:16.309
In December, the Alamo Trust offered

00:02:16.310 --> 00:02:18.349
3.5 million, which can too

00:02:18.350 --> 00:02:20.149
quickly declined.

00:02:20.150 --> 00:02:21.499
They keep alleging that you're not

00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:22.939
negotiating in good faith.

00:02:22.940 --> 00:02:23.749
What do you say to that?

00:02:23.750 --> 00:02:25.579
All lies. They've never called me.

00:02:25.580 --> 00:02:26.969
So we never really had a negotiation.

00:02:26.970 --> 00:02:28.879
They would send me an email with

00:02:28.880 --> 00:02:29.839
an offer.

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:31.009
I would send them an email back

00:02:31.010 --> 00:02:32.899
saying, "No, thank you," and

00:02:32.900 --> 00:02:34.189
some other words. They've wanted to

00:02:34.190 --> 00:02:35.989
negotiate with me over my property,

00:02:35.990 --> 00:02:37.549
but they wanted a loaded gun to do

00:02:37.550 --> 00:02:39.229
it. They've wanted the threat of

00:02:39.230 --> 00:02:41.329
eminent domain hanging over my head

00:02:41.330 --> 00:02:42.979
for me to take their number instead

00:02:42.980 --> 00:02:45.169
of them taking my number.

00:02:45.170 --> 00:02:46.429
And running a business when you're

00:02:46.430 --> 00:02:47.689
under the threat of eminent domain

00:02:47.690 --> 00:02:49.099
is really, really hard.

00:02:49.100 --> 00:02:50.149
I mean, you know, because you're, as

00:02:50.150 --> 00:02:51.079
a business person, you're looking

00:02:51.080 --> 00:02:53.029
out today,

00:02:53.030 --> 00:02:54.889
tomorrow, a month from

00:02:54.890 --> 00:02:55.849
now, but you're also looking out

00:02:55.850 --> 00:02:57.709
five and ten years out to see

00:02:57.710 --> 00:02:59.219
what you need. You need a new

00:02:59.220 --> 00:03:01.219
system. You need you need to remodel

00:03:01.220 --> 00:03:02.209
the place. You need to put some

00:03:02.210 --> 00:03:04.129
money into it some other way.

00:03:04.130 --> 00:03:05.479
And not knowing whether the

00:03:05.480 --> 00:03:06.349
government was going to come in and

00:03:06.350 --> 00:03:08.689
take it in at any moment

00:03:08.690 --> 00:03:10.519
really kind of defeated the

00:03:10.520 --> 00:03:12.529
whole joy I had about

00:03:12.530 --> 00:03:13.849
thinking about the future of this

00:03:13.850 --> 00:03:15.439
place and in developing ten-year

00:03:15.440 --> 00:03:16.440
strategies.

00:03:17.150 --> 00:03:19.309
A pissed-off Cantu started tacking

00:03:19.310 --> 00:03:21.229
on an extra million dollar fee to

00:03:21.230 --> 00:03:22.759
his offer each year that the

00:03:22.760 --> 00:03:24.049
government threatened him with

00:03:24.050 --> 00:03:25.129
eminent domain.

00:03:25.130 --> 00:03:27.139
And earlier this year, George P.

00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:28.849
Bush, who's the son of Jeb and the

00:03:28.850 --> 00:03:30.739
nephew of George W., called

00:03:30.740 --> 00:03:31.969
Cantu's refusal to sell at the

00:03:31.970 --> 00:03:34.369
state's price "dishonorable."

00:03:34.370 --> 00:03:36.409
I told my wife that if I saw him,

00:03:36.410 --> 00:03:37.789
I would challenge him to a duel in

00:03:37.790 --> 00:03:39.019
front of the Alamo.

00:03:39.020 --> 00:03:40.939
I would use squirt guns, not

00:03:40.940 --> 00:03:41.869
real gun, because I want to kill

00:03:41.870 --> 00:03:43.039
anybody and I don't want to get

00:03:43.040 --> 00:03:44.929
killed. But, you know, I mean,

00:03:44.930 --> 00:03:47.059
just, just to avenge my honor.

00:03:47.060 --> 00:03:48.679
Bush didn't respond to Reason's

00:03:48.680 --> 00:03:50.299
requests for comment.

00:03:50.300 --> 00:03:52.849
Proponents of the Alamo's plan

00:03:52.850 --> 00:03:54.739
would argue that this

00:03:54.740 --> 00:03:56.389
is necessary. It's necessary that

00:03:56.390 --> 00:03:57.979
they take these buildings, that they

00:03:57.980 --> 00:03:59.989
seized them in order to

00:03:59.990 --> 00:04:01.939
expand the, the visitor center

00:04:01.940 --> 00:04:03.289
of the new theater that they're

00:04:03.290 --> 00:04:04.609
building.

00:04:04.610 --> 00:04:07.159
What do you say to those people who

00:04:07.160 --> 00:04:09.049
are supporters of the Alamo really

00:04:09.050 --> 00:04:10.219
expanding their footprint in the

00:04:10.220 --> 00:04:10.729
city?

00:04:10.730 --> 00:04:11.902
Well, those people that say that,

00:04:11.903 --> 00:04:13.789
that support that,

00:04:13.790 --> 00:04:15.199
are the ones that read in the paper

00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:16.549
that I would not come to the table.

00:04:16.550 --> 00:04:18.319
But the truth is, is that I've told

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:20.208
the museum people for six years that

00:04:20.209 --> 00:04:21.229
I would come to the table.

00:04:21.230 --> 00:04:22.699
I've been waiting for six years for

00:04:22.700 --> 00:04:24.589
my phone to ring for, for

00:04:24.590 --> 00:04:25.849
them to sit down and have an honest

00:04:25.850 --> 00:04:27.289
negotiation with me.

00:04:27.290 --> 00:04:28.699
I've never been in the way of what

00:04:28.700 --> 00:04:30.979
they wanted to do. So I would say,

00:04:30.980 --> 00:04:32.479
how could I be in the way of

00:04:32.480 --> 00:04:33.889
something when I told them I would

00:04:33.890 --> 00:04:35.629
sell to them from day one?

00:04:35.630 --> 00:04:37.009
They just never have wanted to meet

00:04:37.010 --> 00:04:39.019
me even close to my price.

00:04:39.020 --> 00:04:40.909
And that's the government saying

00:04:40.910 --> 00:04:42.199
we don't have to because we can

00:04:42.200 --> 00:04:44.149
eminent domain you instead.

00:04:44.150 --> 00:04:45.979
Cantu says that when he started

00:04:45.980 --> 00:04:47.449
Moses Rose's, it was in a

00:04:47.450 --> 00:04:49.159
dilapidated part of town.

00:04:49.160 --> 00:04:50.929
He and his family are being denied

00:04:50.930 --> 00:04:52.819
the opportunity to reap the rewards

00:04:52.820 --> 00:04:55.789
of more than a decade of sacrifice.

00:04:55.790 --> 00:04:57.499
This part of downtown San Antonio

00:04:57.500 --> 00:04:59.629
was not a place anybody really came.

00:04:59.630 --> 00:05:00.919
It was a bunch of homeless people

00:05:00.920 --> 00:05:01.920
here.

00:05:02.340 --> 00:05:04.339
My idea was to open up a bar

00:05:04.340 --> 00:05:05.959
and grill and

00:05:07.220 --> 00:05:08.899
have live music, but most of the

00:05:08.900 --> 00:05:11.209
people that played for me

00:05:11.210 --> 00:05:13.009
at first were just homeless guys

00:05:13.010 --> 00:05:14.419
with guitars. I mean, that's really

00:05:14.420 --> 00:05:15.559
kind of what we had over here,

00:05:15.560 --> 00:05:16.789
really. And then after a while, it

00:05:16.790 --> 00:05:18.109
just kind of started clicking.

00:05:18.110 --> 00:05:19.489
Downtown started opening up a little

00:05:19.490 --> 00:05:21.439
bit, and this part of downtown

00:05:21.440 --> 00:05:22.429
started getting a little bit more

00:05:22.430 --> 00:05:24.499
gentrified and a little bit better.

00:05:24.500 --> 00:05:26.449
The San Antonio City Council voted

00:05:26.450 --> 00:05:28.339
in late January to authorize

00:05:28.340 --> 00:05:30.199
the use of eminent domain, which

00:05:30.200 --> 00:05:31.939
would allow the city to condemn and

00:05:31.940 --> 00:05:33.829
acquire the property to hand to the

00:05:33.830 --> 00:05:35.779
Alamo Trust if Cantu doesn't

00:05:35.780 --> 00:05:37.429
take their state-backed offer.

00:05:39.620 --> 00:05:41.509
After our interview, Cantu met with

00:05:41.510 --> 00:05:43.129
the trust's attorneys.

00:05:43.130 --> 00:05:44.929
He says they offered him 2.4

00:05:44.930 --> 00:05:47.269
million, more than $1,000,000

00:05:47.270 --> 00:05:48.649
less than what they'd offered him

00:05:48.650 --> 00:05:50.269
before the city started the eminent

00:05:50.270 --> 00:05:51.349
domain process.

00:05:51.350 --> 00:05:53.269
It was just a bad faith

00:05:53.270 --> 00:05:55.379
bullshit negotiation that they

00:05:55.380 --> 00:05:57.299
said they had to have

00:05:57.300 --> 00:05:58.409
before they would start eminent

00:05:58.410 --> 00:05:59.519
domain.

00:05:59.520 --> 00:06:01.949
Cantu has vowed to keep fighting.

00:06:01.950 --> 00:06:03.929
Texan is small government

00:06:03.930 --> 00:06:06.059
and, and fiercely

00:06:06.060 --> 00:06:08.489
independent. It's stupidly ironic.

00:06:08.490 --> 00:06:09.490
Completely un-Texan.

